1
00:00:02,135 --> 00:00:03,375
GORDON: <i>Previously on</i> Gotham...

2
00:00:04,338 --> 00:00:06,967
Where is Xander Wilde?

3
00:00:08,842 --> 00:00:09,969
My God.

4
00:00:10,177 --> 00:00:11,372
<i>There's two of them.</i>

5
00:00:11,612 --> 00:00:14,309
I'm gonna drive
you mad, brother.

6
00:00:14,381 --> 00:00:16,646
All of Gotham will
be joining you, too.

7
00:00:16,984 --> 00:00:19,852
You shall become
the Demon's Head.

8
00:00:21,855 --> 00:00:23,756
She's got the mark
of the Demon's Head.

9
00:00:23,857 --> 00:00:26,588
No woman has ever been allowed
to lead the League of Shadows.

10
00:00:28,729 --> 00:00:31,665
The sisters of the League
are yours to command.

11
00:00:32,466 --> 00:00:33,832
Tell me what I need to know.

12
00:00:34,835 --> 00:00:35,835
(GROANING)

13
00:00:35,969 --> 00:00:38,564
BRUCE: <i>I could have
killed Jerome, and I didn't.</i>

14
00:00:39,306 --> 00:00:42,708
Don't take so much responsibility
that you get yourself killed.

15
00:00:44,378 --> 00:00:48,782
JEROME: <i>I came up with a plan
to turn this city into a madhouse.</i>

16
00:00:52,286 --> 00:00:54,585
Oh, we're gonna
need a lot more of this!

17
00:00:58,091 --> 00:00:59,956
Thank you all for
coming this evening.

18
00:01:00,060 --> 00:01:01,756
As your interim mayor,

19
00:01:01,862 --> 00:01:05,094
I know my recent
appointment was sudden,

20
00:01:05,198 --> 00:01:08,657
and perhaps a bit
of a shock to some.

21
00:01:08,735 --> 00:01:10,203
Quite frankly, I was shocked.

22
00:01:10,270 --> 00:01:13,502
What is important now is
the future of this great city.

23
00:01:13,574 --> 00:01:15,566
That is why I'm
meeting with all of you.

24
00:01:15,676 --> 00:01:22,082
Well, Mayor, as chairperson of
Gotham's Moral Authority Society,

25
00:01:22,149 --> 00:01:26,280
our members have been,
quite frankly, unnerved

26
00:01:26,386 --> 00:01:30,448
by the recent going-ons
in our great city.

27
00:01:30,557 --> 00:01:33,049
We have seen
criminals take office,

28
00:01:33,126 --> 00:01:35,789
gunfights in our
streets, corruption...

29
00:01:35,896 --> 00:01:37,626
Mrs. Haverstock.

30
00:01:37,731 --> 00:01:41,566
The Commissioner and I have
worked tirelessly these past few weeks

31
00:01:41,635 --> 00:01:44,730
to improve the way
this city conducts itself.

32
00:01:47,574 --> 00:01:49,440
Wyatt, everything all right?

33
00:01:49,576 --> 00:01:50,942
We're looking into it now, sir.

34
00:01:51,278 --> 00:01:53,679
Did a window blow open?

35
00:01:53,780 --> 00:01:55,681
It's gotten so cold.

36
00:01:59,419 --> 00:02:00,419
(BOTH LADIES GASP)

37
00:02:00,621 --> 00:02:02,501
- What's happened?
- MAN: Don't come any closer.

38
00:02:03,323 --> 00:02:04,552
No!

39
00:02:09,396 --> 00:02:10,396
(SHUDDERING)

40
00:02:19,006 --> 00:02:20,030
(SCREAMING)

41
00:02:20,140 --> 00:02:21,472
Good evening, everyone.

42
00:02:22,709 --> 00:02:23,709
(GASPING)

43
00:02:25,345 --> 00:02:26,779
What do you want with us?

44
00:02:26,847 --> 00:02:29,282
Sorry, no time for
questions, Mr. Mayor.

45
00:02:29,549 --> 00:02:33,213
You see, your presence is
urgently needed elsewhere.

46
00:02:33,887 --> 00:02:37,688
Whatever you expect
as ransom, I will double it.

47
00:02:41,461 --> 00:02:44,090
I have access to the
police pension fund.

48
00:02:44,965 --> 00:02:47,833
Wow, that could
be a lot of money.

49
00:02:47,934 --> 00:02:52,030
Tempting, but no thanks.

50
00:02:52,639 --> 00:02:54,039
Bridgit, isn't it?

51
00:02:54,141 --> 00:02:56,838
I can get you safe
passage from the city,

52
00:02:56,910 --> 00:02:58,538
money, a new home...

53
00:02:58,645 --> 00:03:02,013
It was people like you that
locked me up in Strange's lab,

54
00:03:02,082 --> 00:03:05,314
and thanks to that, there
is no Bridgit anymore.

55
00:03:05,385 --> 00:03:07,217
I can get you a pardon, son.

56
00:03:07,320 --> 00:03:10,119
All will be forgiven.
Just stop this lunatic.

57
00:03:10,190 --> 00:03:12,716
Lunatic's a little harsh.

58
00:03:12,959 --> 00:03:15,121
I prefer "visionary."

59
00:03:15,495 --> 00:03:18,329
Oswald, can't you do something?

60
00:03:21,034 --> 00:03:22,034
Afraid not.

61
00:03:22,369 --> 00:03:26,033
I am with Mr. Valeska 100%.

62
00:03:26,106 --> 00:03:29,076
Every cop in this city
will be looking for us,

63
00:03:29,176 --> 00:03:30,439
and when they find you,

64
00:03:30,544 --> 00:03:33,412
expect no mercy,
just a hail of bullets.

65
00:03:33,513 --> 00:03:34,879
So serious.

66
00:03:35,382 --> 00:03:38,147
That's why your approval
ratings are so low.

67
00:03:38,218 --> 00:03:39,846
Hey, tell you what.

68
00:03:39,920 --> 00:03:43,584
Try threatening me again,
but this time, try it with a smile.

69
00:03:45,092 --> 00:03:47,084
Oh! See, this is what's wrong.

70
00:03:47,194 --> 00:03:50,323
Nobody knows how to
have fun anymore, right?

71
00:03:50,397 --> 00:03:53,367
But see our friend
down there, bag head?

72
00:03:54,101 --> 00:03:55,899
He's figured out a
way to solve that.

73
00:03:59,473 --> 00:04:00,513
(STUTTERING AND SCREAMING)

74
00:04:02,642 --> 00:04:03,642
(GROANING)

75
00:04:07,147 --> 00:04:08,171
(LAUGHING MANIACALLY)

76
00:04:10,751 --> 00:04:13,346
It's time to give this
city the boost it needs.

77
00:04:13,453 --> 00:04:16,446
Time to stop taking
ourselves so seriously.

78
00:04:16,556 --> 00:04:20,391
I mean, come on, Gotham,
what do you have to lose?

79
00:04:23,797 --> 00:04:25,163
Except your sanity.

80
00:04:27,334 --> 00:04:28,374
(BOTH LAUGHING MANIACALLY)

81
00:04:36,309 --> 00:04:38,778
You gonna tell me why we needed
to come to the garage, Alfred?

82
00:04:38,945 --> 00:04:41,744
Happy birthday, Master Wayne.

83
00:04:42,983 --> 00:04:44,076
You remembered.

84
00:04:44,551 --> 00:04:45,985
Of course I remembered.

85
00:04:46,653 --> 00:04:48,281
I bloody love your birthdays.

86
00:04:48,889 --> 00:04:51,051
Your seventh was
an absolute blinder.

87
00:04:51,124 --> 00:04:53,102
Yeah, I remember you had
about 50 kids come up here,

88
00:04:53,126 --> 00:04:55,755
but you were off
outside on your own.

89
00:04:55,829 --> 00:04:58,993
You were obsessed by this
one gift that your dad gave you,

90
00:04:59,099 --> 00:05:00,465
this bright red wagon.

91
00:05:01,034 --> 00:05:02,979
You were in the garden all
day, collecting all these rocks.

92
00:05:03,003 --> 00:05:04,847
When I asked you, "What are
you gonna do with these rocks?"

93
00:05:04,871 --> 00:05:10,401
You said, "I'm gonna
build a home for my wagon.

94
00:05:10,777 --> 00:05:13,906
"A secret place that
only I know about."

95
00:05:27,694 --> 00:05:28,694
What's this?

96
00:05:28,795 --> 00:05:31,675
Well, it's the reason why I brought
you down to the garage, Master Bruce.

97
00:05:35,168 --> 00:05:36,168
(CAR STARTING)

98
00:05:40,574 --> 00:05:42,167
Alfred, I don't
know what to say.

99
00:05:44,444 --> 00:05:47,972
V8, five-liter,
460-horsepower engine.

100
00:05:48,148 --> 00:05:50,549
Painted matte
black, anti-reflective,

101
00:05:50,650 --> 00:05:52,141
very difficult to see at night.

102
00:05:52,219 --> 00:05:53,619
Oh, and of course this...

103
00:05:55,488 --> 00:05:57,252
100% bulletproof.

104
00:06:00,193 --> 00:06:01,855
Best be prepared, eh?

105
00:06:09,669 --> 00:06:10,669
(CHUCKLES)

106
00:06:11,171 --> 00:06:12,400
Oh, mate.

107
00:06:18,879 --> 00:06:20,745
HARVEY: Jim, hey, what gives?

108
00:06:20,881 --> 00:06:23,578
The mayor and the police commissioner
have been kidnapped by Jerome.

109
00:06:23,850 --> 00:06:26,547
Got every cop in the city out
there searching all the spots

110
00:06:26,653 --> 00:06:28,178
Jerome has been
seen the last week.

111
00:06:28,255 --> 00:06:29,689
You got something for me?

112
00:06:29,890 --> 00:06:32,758
I was gonna say I just won
100 bucks in the scratch-off lotto

113
00:06:32,859 --> 00:06:35,140
at the liquor store, and we
could go to the track with it,

114
00:06:35,195 --> 00:06:37,426
but you can do your thing first.

115
00:06:37,530 --> 00:06:39,624
- Gordon.
- PENGUIN: <i>We need to talk.</i>

116
00:06:40,734 --> 00:06:43,533
- Oswald?
- I'm out back. Come alone.

117
00:06:46,940 --> 00:06:48,272
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

118
00:06:49,209 --> 00:06:50,233
GORDON: All right.

119
00:06:54,247 --> 00:06:55,545
Well, this is a first.

120
00:06:55,615 --> 00:06:57,550
Are you doing
anything about Jerome?

121
00:06:57,617 --> 00:06:58,915
We're looking for him.

122
00:06:59,286 --> 00:07:00,379
Do you know where he is?

123
00:07:00,453 --> 00:07:02,653
And if I did, do you really
think I would just tell you?

124
00:07:02,789 --> 00:07:04,883
Have you march in
there, guns blazing?

125
00:07:04,958 --> 00:07:06,324
He needs to be stopped.

126
00:07:06,559 --> 00:07:08,755
He has everyone under his thumb.

127
00:07:08,828 --> 00:07:10,820
Freeze, Firefly, Hatter.

128
00:07:10,931 --> 00:07:14,163
They are all part of his
plan. A dark, terrible plan.

129
00:07:14,267 --> 00:07:15,291
Which is?

130
00:07:16,136 --> 00:07:18,696
Scarecrow has
made a gas for him.

131
00:07:18,772 --> 00:07:20,764
- Like the fear toxin?
- Worse.

132
00:07:20,974 --> 00:07:22,067
Much worse.

133
00:07:22,242 --> 00:07:26,236
I saw it turn someone into a
maniacal, cackling, violent animal.

134
00:07:26,313 --> 00:07:27,645
What does he plan to do with it?

135
00:07:28,648 --> 00:07:31,345
He's smart. He hasn't shared
the details of his plans with anyone.

136
00:07:31,451 --> 00:07:33,784
Instead, we all have a
separate task to perform.

137
00:07:34,087 --> 00:07:35,180
Such as?

138
00:07:35,855 --> 00:07:37,323
He has yet to give me my role.

139
00:07:37,624 --> 00:07:39,616
Why did you come here if
you're not gonna help me?

140
00:07:39,693 --> 00:07:41,685
He scares the living
hell out of me, okay?

141
00:07:43,530 --> 00:07:46,989
I mean, I was willing to play
along with him for a while.

142
00:07:47,233 --> 00:07:48,997
Perhaps he had a
way to make us all rich,

143
00:07:49,102 --> 00:07:51,230
or return to the good
old days, you know.

144
00:07:51,671 --> 00:07:53,435
But nothing good
will come of this.

145
00:07:53,573 --> 00:07:55,474
Or maybe you just
don't like the competition.

146
00:07:56,443 --> 00:07:58,139
Jerome casts quite the shadow.

147
00:07:58,244 --> 00:08:00,076
Oh, please.

148
00:08:00,280 --> 00:08:03,011
He's a maniac. An anarchist.

149
00:08:03,116 --> 00:08:06,382
He is not interested
in money or power.

150
00:08:07,354 --> 00:08:09,346
And I am an
honest criminal, Jim.

151
00:08:09,456 --> 00:08:11,789
Where is he? Where is the gas?

152
00:08:11,858 --> 00:08:13,952
He only tells you
what he needs to,

153
00:08:14,027 --> 00:08:15,290
when he needs to.

154
00:08:15,662 --> 00:08:17,426
I just know he
has to be stopped.

155
00:08:17,664 --> 00:08:19,132
HARVEY: Jim, hey!

156
00:08:19,366 --> 00:08:20,629
You down here?

157
00:08:21,001 --> 00:08:22,629
- Jim?
- Yup.

158
00:08:23,636 --> 00:08:26,765
Hey, a uni just spotted
Jerome near Paisley Square.

159
00:08:26,940 --> 00:08:27,999
All right, let's go.

160
00:08:28,641 --> 00:08:29,641
(ROCK MUSIC PLAYING)

161
00:08:30,977 --> 00:08:31,977
(CROWD CHEERING)

162
00:08:32,278 --> 00:08:34,247
(SINGING "TIME HAS COME TODAY")

163
00:08:47,394 --> 00:08:48,692
Hey, what's happening to my mic?

164
00:08:48,928 --> 00:08:51,329
Hey, buddy, beat it, will
you? I'm trying to work here.

165
00:08:52,432 --> 00:08:53,432
Whoo!

166
00:08:57,070 --> 00:08:58,350
- (SINGER GRUNTS)
- (CROWD GASPS)

167
00:09:01,041 --> 00:09:02,441
Where's everyone going?

168
00:09:03,576 --> 00:09:04,576
(CROWD SCREAMING)

169
00:09:04,978 --> 00:09:07,914
Ladies and gentlemen, we
are the Arkham Asylum Lunatics,

170
00:09:08,014 --> 00:09:10,813
and we came here
to blow some minds!

171
00:09:12,318 --> 00:09:15,482
Sorry to interrupt
your little show.

172
00:09:15,889 --> 00:09:18,188
But you are gonna
love this next one.

173
00:09:18,691 --> 00:09:21,559
Introducing Mayor Pritchard,

174
00:09:21,861 --> 00:09:23,386
Commissioner Reynolds,

175
00:09:23,863 --> 00:09:27,732
Archbishop McGregor,
and this lady.

176
00:09:28,168 --> 00:09:29,431
Whoever she is.

177
00:09:29,769 --> 00:09:31,032
This is everybody.

178
00:09:31,104 --> 00:09:33,096
Everybody, say hi.

179
00:09:34,040 --> 00:09:36,134
Now, as you can see,

180
00:09:36,242 --> 00:09:38,370
we're still waiting for
two guests of honor.

181
00:09:38,745 --> 00:09:39,974
But in the meantime,

182
00:09:40,146 --> 00:09:43,412
let's go over the rules of
tonight's entertainment, shall we?

183
00:09:44,417 --> 00:09:45,417
Dynamite.

184
00:09:46,653 --> 00:09:47,814
Trigger.

185
00:09:48,588 --> 00:09:50,216
I don't get what I want,

186
00:09:50,390 --> 00:09:51,414
boom.

187
00:09:51,491 --> 00:09:52,925
Headless people.

188
00:09:53,326 --> 00:09:56,057
And if any of you are
thinking of going anywhere,

189
00:09:56,129 --> 00:09:57,563
you'll die, too.

190
00:09:58,631 --> 00:10:01,567
Now, the one man who
can get me what I want.

191
00:10:03,169 --> 00:10:04,728
Calling Gordon.

192
00:10:05,605 --> 00:10:09,042
Calling Captain James Gordon.

193
00:10:09,242 --> 00:10:10,242
(LAUGHING MANIACALLY)

194
00:10:15,782 --> 00:10:18,149
I speak on behalf of myself

195
00:10:18,751 --> 00:10:21,277
and all other gang
leaders in this city

196
00:10:21,454 --> 00:10:24,891
when I say your
arrogance and disrespect

197
00:10:25,492 --> 00:10:27,984
will no longer be tolerated.

198
00:10:28,895 --> 00:10:32,991
You beat and then dragged
my brother from here

199
00:10:33,099 --> 00:10:34,658
like a dog.

200
00:10:35,001 --> 00:10:36,594
Your brother's an ass.

201
00:10:37,537 --> 00:10:40,507
He abuses our staff and
refuses to pay his exorbitant tab.

202
00:10:40,607 --> 00:10:42,473
He is my brother,

203
00:10:42,542 --> 00:10:44,807
and he demands your respect.

204
00:10:45,044 --> 00:10:48,105
And I suppose an apology
would be out of the question.

205
00:10:48,715 --> 00:10:49,715
(CHUCKLES)

206
00:10:50,216 --> 00:10:53,778
Your blood will be his apology.

207
00:10:55,455 --> 00:10:56,455
Thought so.

208
00:11:01,728 --> 00:11:02,728
(MEN GRUNTING)

209
00:11:13,039 --> 00:11:14,337
I could have handled them.

210
00:11:14,707 --> 00:11:17,871
That's the advantage of having
your own personal army, Tabs.

211
00:11:17,977 --> 00:11:19,172
You don't have to.

212
00:11:20,146 --> 00:11:21,444
Isn't that right?

213
00:11:26,819 --> 00:11:27,843
What's wrong?

214
00:11:28,388 --> 00:11:30,186
Ra's al Ghul chose you,

215
00:11:30,623 --> 00:11:32,285
no one else, to
pass on his spirit.

216
00:11:32,492 --> 00:11:35,223
We will serve you,
protect you, of course,

217
00:11:35,328 --> 00:11:37,354
but surely you intend
to continue his legacy,

218
00:11:37,463 --> 00:11:39,694
and not just remain
here in this place.

219
00:11:39,866 --> 00:11:41,061
What does that mean?

220
00:11:43,369 --> 00:11:44,928
"Continue his legacy."

221
00:11:45,838 --> 00:11:47,329
I like the sound of that.

222
00:11:48,208 --> 00:11:49,574
As I told you,

223
00:11:50,410 --> 00:11:52,538
we have much more to show you.

224
00:11:54,113 --> 00:11:55,240
Are you ready?

225
00:11:55,682 --> 00:11:56,741
Yes.

226
00:12:08,061 --> 00:12:09,261
GUARD: What the hell was that?

227
00:12:09,295 --> 00:12:10,295
(TIMER BEEPING)

228
00:12:15,068 --> 00:12:16,068
(BOTH SCREAMING)

229
00:12:25,745 --> 00:12:28,078
Gentlemen, ladies,

230
00:12:28,181 --> 00:12:31,845
your assistance is
urgently required.

231
00:12:32,285 --> 00:12:34,516
Be careful, these are
very dangerous materials.

232
00:12:34,587 --> 00:12:35,850
We're counting on it.

233
00:12:37,690 --> 00:12:41,422
More laughing gas,
we need to make.

234
00:12:44,230 --> 00:12:46,222
There's no time to waste.

235
00:12:46,666 --> 00:12:48,760
We need it in bulk, you see.

236
00:12:49,836 --> 00:12:51,634
Well... Well, how
much of it do you need?

237
00:12:54,507 --> 00:12:55,507
Oh!

238
00:12:55,608 --> 00:12:57,076
CRANE: This much.

239
00:13:00,146 --> 00:13:01,146
(ROCK MUSIC PLAYING)

240
00:13:12,759 --> 00:13:15,285
JEROME: Ladies and
gentlemen, as I live and breathe,

241
00:13:15,595 --> 00:13:17,564
James Gordon is in the house.

242
00:13:20,733 --> 00:13:23,100
I'm not talking to you
until I can get up there

243
00:13:23,169 --> 00:13:25,297
and check on the
well-being of your hostages.

244
00:13:25,805 --> 00:13:27,967
JEROME: First of
all, Jim, you're late.

245
00:13:28,274 --> 00:13:32,575
Secondly, I think I'm the one
who should be making demands.

246
00:13:32,645 --> 00:13:33,645
Don't you?

247
00:13:33,780 --> 00:13:36,750
What you're doing is
an act of terror, Valeska.

248
00:13:37,583 --> 00:13:40,314
Ask our mayor what
this city's policy is

249
00:13:40,420 --> 00:13:42,116
on negotiating with terrorists.

250
00:13:42,188 --> 00:13:43,417
"Terrorists"?

251
00:13:44,023 --> 00:13:45,992
Frankly, I'm
offended. No, no, no.

252
00:13:47,026 --> 00:13:48,146
That's close enough, Gordon.

253
00:13:48,728 --> 00:13:49,728
(CROWD SCREAMING)

254
00:13:53,466 --> 00:13:55,560
JEROME: And none of
you go anywhere, either.

255
00:14:01,207 --> 00:14:02,675
Dead man's trigger.

256
00:14:03,910 --> 00:14:05,378
This falls out of my hand

257
00:14:05,478 --> 00:14:08,038
for any reason, and... Bang!

258
00:14:08,414 --> 00:14:09,414
(CROWD GASPS)

259
00:14:11,751 --> 00:14:13,379
I got two empty chairs here.

260
00:14:13,986 --> 00:14:16,114
You haven't even asked
me who they're for yet.

261
00:14:16,389 --> 00:14:18,324
All right. I'll bite.
Who are they for?

262
00:14:18,391 --> 00:14:19,882
Come on, James.

263
00:14:19,992 --> 00:14:21,119
You're a detective.

264
00:14:21,961 --> 00:14:23,156
Do some detecting.

265
00:14:25,298 --> 00:14:26,891
Jeremiah, your brother.

266
00:14:27,867 --> 00:14:29,802
Bingo. That's one.

267
00:14:30,236 --> 00:14:31,465
And the other?

268
00:14:31,537 --> 00:14:33,403
Well, the only other
irksome do-gooder

269
00:14:33,506 --> 00:14:35,532
who's ever spoiled
my fun in this town.

270
00:14:37,844 --> 00:14:39,472
Bruce Wayne.

271
00:14:41,314 --> 00:14:42,407
No.

272
00:14:43,149 --> 00:14:44,310
No?

273
00:14:44,417 --> 00:14:45,908
You can take me.

274
00:14:46,519 --> 00:14:48,852
I'll sit up there with one of
those things around my neck,

275
00:14:48,921 --> 00:14:50,355
but I won't let you have him.

276
00:14:50,690 --> 00:14:53,524
Oh, I don't want you, Jim.

277
00:14:54,594 --> 00:14:55,926
I want my brother,

278
00:14:56,295 --> 00:14:57,786
and I want Bruce.

279
00:14:58,097 --> 00:14:59,292
I want them now.

280
00:14:59,399 --> 00:15:02,426
All right, let me get these people
out of here, I'll come up there...

281
00:15:02,535 --> 00:15:04,060
You are not listening to me.

282
00:15:04,971 --> 00:15:07,202
And that is forcing my hand.

283
00:15:11,778 --> 00:15:12,905
Jerome.

284
00:15:14,447 --> 00:15:15,779
- (DETONATOR BUZZING)
- No!

285
00:15:17,316 --> 00:15:18,340
(CROWD SCREAMING)

286
00:15:24,724 --> 00:15:26,249
JEROME: Bring me my brother.

287
00:15:27,093 --> 00:15:28,459
Bring me Wayne.

288
00:15:30,463 --> 00:15:31,761
Bring them now.

289
00:15:39,272 --> 00:15:40,592
(ALFRED SINGING
"HAPPY BIRTHDAY")

290
00:15:47,046 --> 00:15:48,446
I'll get some plates.

291
00:15:54,954 --> 00:15:59,824
You know, for a billionaire,
your security system is lame.

292
00:15:59,926 --> 00:16:00,985
Miss Kyle.

293
00:16:01,861 --> 00:16:03,090
BRUCE: Thank you, Alfred.

294
00:16:03,162 --> 00:16:04,323
Enjoy.

295
00:16:09,302 --> 00:16:10,463
Thank you.

296
00:16:10,937 --> 00:16:12,098
For what?

297
00:16:13,139 --> 00:16:14,664
Visiting me on my birthday.

298
00:16:14,941 --> 00:16:15,941
Oh!

299
00:16:16,442 --> 00:16:18,377
I actually didn't know
it was your birthday,

300
00:16:18,478 --> 00:16:21,312
I just happened to be
strolling in the neighborhood.

301
00:16:22,815 --> 00:16:25,512
Either way, it's
good to see you.

302
00:16:34,961 --> 00:16:36,452
I knew it was an act.

303
00:16:38,464 --> 00:16:39,488
What?

304
00:16:40,099 --> 00:16:41,362
The brat,

305
00:16:41,467 --> 00:16:44,301
and the drinking, the friends.

306
00:16:44,470 --> 00:16:45,836
It was an act.

307
00:16:48,107 --> 00:16:49,973
I think you're more
sure about that than me.

308
00:16:52,078 --> 00:16:53,307
Master Bruce,

309
00:16:53,379 --> 00:16:54,677
we have visitors.

310
00:16:54,981 --> 00:16:56,244
Bruce, we need your help.

311
00:16:57,049 --> 00:16:58,210
BRUCE: What happened?

312
00:17:00,186 --> 00:17:03,088
<i>Don't you know it's rude
to keep a guy waiting?</i>

313
00:17:03,823 --> 00:17:05,849
<i>Bring me my hostages, James.</i>

314
00:17:05,925 --> 00:17:09,418
<i>My trigger finger
is getting itchy.</i>

315
00:17:10,863 --> 00:17:14,231
The hostages he wants
are his brother and you.

316
00:17:15,001 --> 00:17:16,867
What, you're having a
laugh. No bloody way.

317
00:17:16,936 --> 00:17:18,700
I don't like it any
more than you do,

318
00:17:18,771 --> 00:17:20,103
but, Bruce, you
have to trust me.

319
00:17:20,339 --> 00:17:21,671
Lucius and I have a plan.

320
00:17:21,741 --> 00:17:22,902
JEROME: <i>You know what?</i>

321
00:17:23,476 --> 00:17:25,741
<i>I don't think you're taking
me seriously enough.</i>

322
00:17:26,178 --> 00:17:28,340
<i>Well, all right.</i>

323
00:17:29,715 --> 00:17:31,047
<i>Let's see.</i>

324
00:17:31,150 --> 00:17:33,142
(IN SING-SONG VOICE)
<i>Eenie, meeny, miny, mo.</i>

325
00:17:33,219 --> 00:17:35,814
<i>One of these
people got to... Go.</i>

326
00:17:39,692 --> 00:17:41,490
<i>Oh, it's that guy.</i>

327
00:17:41,827 --> 00:17:42,851
<i>Oh, well.</i>

328
00:17:44,664 --> 00:17:45,741
Did you see what just happened?

329
00:17:45,765 --> 00:17:48,166
That man's a raving bloody
lunatic. He can't be trusted.

330
00:17:48,234 --> 00:17:49,497
For once, I agree with Alfred.

331
00:17:49,569 --> 00:17:50,764
Bruce, listen to me.

332
00:17:51,203 --> 00:17:53,229
With your help, we can
prevent more deaths.

333
00:17:57,376 --> 00:17:58,537
What's the plan?

334
00:18:00,246 --> 00:18:02,477
Jerome is using a
short-wave radio trigger

335
00:18:02,582 --> 00:18:03,641
with a dead man's switch.

336
00:18:03,749 --> 00:18:04,773
If we can cut the signal,

337
00:18:04,884 --> 00:18:06,528
he won't be able to
activate the explosives.

338
00:18:06,552 --> 00:18:07,884
This emits a powerful signal

339
00:18:07,954 --> 00:18:09,889
that disables all
radio waves close to it.

340
00:18:09,956 --> 00:18:11,948
Once within a few
feet of Jerome's device,

341
00:18:12,058 --> 00:18:13,219
his trigger will be useless.

342
00:18:13,292 --> 00:18:14,885
It will give us the
time for the snipers

343
00:18:14,961 --> 00:18:17,123
to get a clean shot on
Jerome, Firefly, and the others.

344
00:18:17,229 --> 00:18:18,807
If I wear this, then that gives
you time to take them out?

345
00:18:18,831 --> 00:18:19,924
Correct.

346
00:18:19,999 --> 00:18:21,262
Are you sure it's gonna work?

347
00:18:22,001 --> 00:18:23,230
I'm positive.

348
00:18:24,403 --> 00:18:25,928
99% positive.

349
00:18:27,707 --> 00:18:28,868
What are we waiting for?

350
00:18:28,941 --> 00:18:30,068
Those people need our help.

351
00:18:30,276 --> 00:18:31,471
Good man.

352
00:18:36,582 --> 00:18:39,780
LELIA: Ra's owned this house
for as long as the city has existed.

353
00:18:41,153 --> 00:18:42,951
He said he kept
his secrets in here.

354
00:18:43,155 --> 00:18:44,646
Ancient secrets.

355
00:18:45,591 --> 00:18:48,288
None of us have ever
seen what's behind this door.

356
00:18:48,628 --> 00:18:50,062
It remains locked.

357
00:18:50,630 --> 00:18:52,155
And there is no key.

358
00:18:52,965 --> 00:18:54,160
Tried dynamite?

359
00:18:56,769 --> 00:18:57,964
No need.

360
00:19:03,609 --> 00:19:05,669
Our master chose
you for a reason.

361
00:19:24,864 --> 00:19:25,864
(DOOR UNLOCKING)

362
00:20:05,438 --> 00:20:06,438
(CHUCKLES SOFTLY)

363
00:20:14,080 --> 00:20:15,446
BARBARA: All my life,

364
00:20:16,682 --> 00:20:19,618
I have known that I
was meant for more,

365
00:20:21,353 --> 00:20:24,517
that there was something deep
inside of me that I couldn't explain.

366
00:20:42,441 --> 00:20:43,602
I'm home.

367
00:20:48,013 --> 00:20:49,173
(INDISTINCT CHATTER ON RADIO)

368
00:20:53,586 --> 00:20:55,026
SNIPER: Sir, we
got target in sight.

369
00:20:56,088 --> 00:20:57,852
<i>No way in from below the stage.</i>

370
00:20:58,457 --> 00:21:00,255
<i>Four of my men
have found positions.</i>

371
00:21:00,359 --> 00:21:02,555
Good. Stay low, hang tight.

372
00:21:02,628 --> 00:21:03,789
No hair triggers.

373
00:21:04,096 --> 00:21:06,122
One missed shot
means <i>adiós</i> Mayor.

374
00:21:06,665 --> 00:21:07,894
SNIPER: <i>Copy that.</i>

375
00:21:08,400 --> 00:21:09,595
Standing by.

376
00:21:10,770 --> 00:21:13,569
I watched the news. I know
why you're here, Mr. Gordon.

377
00:21:13,639 --> 00:21:15,107
And you must be out of your mind

378
00:21:15,174 --> 00:21:17,769
if you think I'm gonna be
led like a lamb to slaughter.

379
00:21:17,843 --> 00:21:20,813
I understand your concern,
but your brother doesn't bluff.

380
00:21:21,313 --> 00:21:23,976
If we ignore his demands,
there's no telling what he might do.

381
00:21:24,083 --> 00:21:26,143
We can block his
remote signal with this.

382
00:21:26,519 --> 00:21:28,818
If you and Bruce can get
within a few feet of him,

383
00:21:28,921 --> 00:21:31,254
it will disable his remote.
He'll be a sitting duck.

384
00:21:31,323 --> 00:21:32,791
Our snipers can
take it from there.

385
00:21:32,892 --> 00:21:34,224
JEREMIAH: For
God's sake, Gordon.

386
00:21:34,293 --> 00:21:35,727
You have to know what he wants.

387
00:21:36,128 --> 00:21:39,462
To murder us both
on live television.

388
00:21:40,933 --> 00:21:42,231
BRUCE: Mr. Valeska.

389
00:21:42,301 --> 00:21:43,462
I'm Bruce Wayne.

390
00:21:43,936 --> 00:21:45,404
It's a pleasure to meet you.

391
00:21:46,572 --> 00:21:47,904
Likewise.

392
00:21:47,973 --> 00:21:49,771
I wish the circumstances
were better.

393
00:21:49,842 --> 00:21:51,674
May I ask what it is
you've been working on?

394
00:21:53,345 --> 00:21:57,510
Yeah, it's a compact electrical
engine. It generates power.

395
00:21:57,917 --> 00:22:00,284
Fascinating. How much power?

396
00:22:00,352 --> 00:22:02,981
Just two could light up every
building south of Westford Bridge.

397
00:22:04,356 --> 00:22:05,722
You have a brilliant mind.

398
00:22:06,959 --> 00:22:08,959
And we all hope we can
soon be rid of your brother,

399
00:22:09,028 --> 00:22:11,054
so that you can carry out
your work free from fear.

400
00:22:11,697 --> 00:22:13,666
I understand if you
choose not to help us today,

401
00:22:15,067 --> 00:22:17,229
but I trust that Captain
Gordon and Mr. Fox

402
00:22:17,336 --> 00:22:18,861
will see that no
harm comes to me.

403
00:22:20,005 --> 00:22:21,473
But, even if it does,

404
00:22:23,409 --> 00:22:25,139
maybe by facing Jerome

405
00:22:26,812 --> 00:22:29,748
I can show the people of
Gotham that standing up to terror

406
00:22:29,849 --> 00:22:31,818
is the only way to
take its power away.

407
00:22:41,994 --> 00:22:43,553
JEREMIAH: Well said.

408
00:22:43,896 --> 00:22:44,896
(CELL PHONE RINGING)

409
00:22:48,667 --> 00:22:49,896
- Harvey.
<i>- Hey.</i>

410
00:22:50,002 --> 00:22:51,800
Just got word that
Freeze and Scarecrow

411
00:22:51,871 --> 00:22:54,033
broke into Wayne
Industries' chemical lab.

412
00:22:54,139 --> 00:22:55,383
Jerome's playing
the long game here,

413
00:22:55,407 --> 00:22:57,652
<i>but we're not gonna be sure what
it is unless we get ahead of him.</i>

414
00:22:57,676 --> 00:22:58,700
The gas.

415
00:22:58,811 --> 00:23:01,076
Penguin told me about
a new Scarecrow toxin.

416
00:23:01,180 --> 00:23:03,376
Head over to the lab. We're
on our way to the square.

417
00:23:05,317 --> 00:23:06,410
They've got a weapon.

418
00:23:06,719 --> 00:23:07,846
Poison gas.

419
00:23:08,287 --> 00:23:09,414
Okay, let's go.

420
00:23:10,589 --> 00:23:11,682
Thank you.

421
00:23:18,430 --> 00:23:19,557
You two.

422
00:23:22,601 --> 00:23:23,601
(MAN LAUGHING MANIACALLY)

423
00:23:26,538 --> 00:23:28,473
Hey. Hey, buddy.

424
00:23:29,375 --> 00:23:30,468
What happened?

425
00:23:30,643 --> 00:23:31,770
What's so funny?

426
00:23:31,944 --> 00:23:33,310
No, no, no, don't.

427
00:23:37,216 --> 00:23:38,684
Ma'am, let me help you.

428
00:23:39,551 --> 00:23:40,678
What happened?

429
00:23:40,753 --> 00:23:43,052
They made us
make it. Tons of it.

430
00:23:43,122 --> 00:23:44,283
Where is it?

431
00:23:44,390 --> 00:23:46,586
It's gone. They took it.

432
00:23:48,727 --> 00:23:49,727
(JEROME SINGING)

433
00:23:56,468 --> 00:24:00,030
Well, look who
decided to show up.

434
00:24:00,706 --> 00:24:02,402
We were starting to get nervous,

435
00:24:02,942 --> 00:24:04,376
especially the mayor here.

436
00:24:04,810 --> 00:24:06,244
My guest of honor.

437
00:24:06,745 --> 00:24:09,681
Please, take your
seats on stage.

438
00:24:20,426 --> 00:24:21,450
Come on.

439
00:24:22,194 --> 00:24:23,287
Don't be shy.

440
00:24:24,263 --> 00:24:25,356
It's all right.

441
00:24:30,869 --> 00:24:32,201
JEROME: We don't have all day.

442
00:24:39,411 --> 00:24:41,778
It's activated. Just let
them get a little closer.

443
00:24:42,481 --> 00:24:43,505
On my command.

444
00:24:44,450 --> 00:24:47,147
SNIPER: <i>My men
have all targets in view.</i>

445
00:24:48,087 --> 00:24:49,180
Standing by.

446
00:24:55,627 --> 00:24:56,993
Hi, brother.

447
00:25:08,440 --> 00:25:09,440
Now.

448
00:25:09,842 --> 00:25:11,902
Fire. All targets, fire.

449
00:25:12,911 --> 00:25:13,911
(CROWD SCREAMING)

450
00:25:18,851 --> 00:25:22,219
I had my guys take up the
best vantage points last night.

451
00:25:22,321 --> 00:25:26,884
So they've been watching
your little SWAT team all day.

452
00:25:29,928 --> 00:25:33,057
Now, Bruce, brother dear.

453
00:25:33,665 --> 00:25:35,361
Get up on stage.

454
00:25:37,436 --> 00:25:39,428
Time to get this party
really started, huh?

455
00:25:48,747 --> 00:25:50,079
What are you doing here?

456
00:25:50,182 --> 00:25:51,844
This is a restricted area.

457
00:25:51,917 --> 00:25:54,887
Our cargo is too
precious to waste.

458
00:25:57,556 --> 00:26:00,424
Let me give you something
I like to keep up my sleeves

459
00:26:00,526 --> 00:26:02,085
for times just like these.

460
00:26:02,561 --> 00:26:03,561
(GASPING AND SCREAMING)

461
00:26:06,999 --> 00:26:08,558
Oh, my God!

462
00:26:09,101 --> 00:26:11,093
You can pilot this
contraption alone, sir?

463
00:26:11,203 --> 00:26:12,330
Yes.

464
00:26:12,604 --> 00:26:14,266
Then look into my eyes.

465
00:26:14,440 --> 00:26:15,440
(WATCH TICKING)

466
00:26:21,547 --> 00:26:22,776
The kidnappings.

467
00:26:23,715 --> 00:26:24,978
The concert in the square.

468
00:26:25,284 --> 00:26:26,877
All to draw the biggest crowd,

469
00:26:26,952 --> 00:26:28,580
so we can drop the
laughing gas on them.

470
00:26:29,588 --> 00:26:31,147
This is madness.

471
00:26:32,057 --> 00:26:35,323
I thought you'd appreciate
the beauty of it all.

472
00:26:35,961 --> 00:26:37,327
But Jerome was right.

473
00:26:37,763 --> 00:26:40,164
You know he
anticipated your betrayal?

474
00:26:41,166 --> 00:26:42,225
That's right.

475
00:26:42,568 --> 00:26:44,127
You went to Gordon.

476
00:26:45,637 --> 00:26:46,696
Judas.

477
00:26:49,041 --> 00:26:50,065
Tie him up.

478
00:26:50,142 --> 00:26:51,440
Put him on the blimp.

479
00:26:52,277 --> 00:26:54,246
Jerome wants him to
have a bird's-eye view.

480
00:27:00,986 --> 00:27:04,388
This book tracks Ra's' legacy
dating back nine centuries.

481
00:27:04,723 --> 00:27:06,954
Did you know he not only
overthrew governments,

482
00:27:07,059 --> 00:27:08,721
but infiltrated royal families?

483
00:27:09,428 --> 00:27:11,158
Ra's influenced history.

484
00:27:11,630 --> 00:27:12,996
He was a cult leader.

485
00:27:13,665 --> 00:27:15,258
And he still has
them brainwashed.

486
00:27:15,434 --> 00:27:17,027
And what about me,
am I brainwashed?

487
00:27:18,103 --> 00:27:19,503
There are things written here

488
00:27:19,605 --> 00:27:22,097
that could change the way
we view the past forever.

489
00:27:24,009 --> 00:27:26,478
Perhaps I'm the one to
bring that change to light.

490
00:27:28,847 --> 00:27:29,940
Look.

491
00:27:30,516 --> 00:27:33,350
This book was compiled
by shamans and mystics

492
00:27:33,452 --> 00:27:35,614
from all over Eastern
Asia and the Middle East.

493
00:27:35,687 --> 00:27:37,298
(SCOFFS) "Shamans and
mystics." Give me a break.

494
00:27:37,322 --> 00:27:40,451
It contains formulas for
potions and incantations

495
00:27:40,526 --> 00:27:41,824
set to raise demons.

496
00:27:41,894 --> 00:27:43,863
To curse our enemies
and contact the dead.

497
00:27:43,962 --> 00:27:45,191
This isn't you.

498
00:27:45,297 --> 00:27:47,175
The Barbara I know would
have already sold all of this junk

499
00:27:47,199 --> 00:27:48,827
- to the highest bidder.
- "Junk"?

500
00:27:49,434 --> 00:27:51,198
This is my destiny.

501
00:27:51,436 --> 00:27:53,803
And being with me and
Selina at the club, that isn't?

502
00:27:55,374 --> 00:27:57,002
You begged me
to partner with you.

503
00:27:57,376 --> 00:27:58,969
Can't you see who
that is up there?

504
00:27:59,044 --> 00:28:01,513
That is me and
Ra's 400 years ago.

505
00:28:01,613 --> 00:28:02,774
Oh, please.

506
00:28:02,848 --> 00:28:05,443
- That doesn't even look like you.
- It looks exactly like me.

507
00:28:05,517 --> 00:28:06,610
It is me.

508
00:28:07,519 --> 00:28:10,011
I have finally found
my true purpose.

509
00:28:10,389 --> 00:28:12,858
I'm not gonna let your
jealousy distract me.

510
00:28:12,958 --> 00:28:16,190
Ladies, escort Ms.
Galavan to the street.

511
00:28:16,995 --> 00:28:18,361
I'll show myself out.

512
00:28:18,430 --> 00:28:21,923
Actually, I think it's
time my loyal servants

513
00:28:22,034 --> 00:28:23,366
taught you some manners.

514
00:28:23,435 --> 00:28:24,596
Why don't you do it?

515
00:28:24,703 --> 00:28:27,002
Because I am the one true heir

516
00:28:27,072 --> 00:28:29,507
of an immortal god's
ancient dynasty.

517
00:28:31,243 --> 00:28:34,236
And I don't dirty my fingers
with the likes of you anymore.

518
00:28:45,857 --> 00:28:47,257
JEROME: No parent will admit it.

519
00:28:47,893 --> 00:28:50,021
But everyone's
got their favorites.

520
00:28:51,096 --> 00:28:52,758
Right, brother?

521
00:28:58,770 --> 00:29:00,705
The one who cleans their room,

522
00:29:01,039 --> 00:29:04,271
does their homework,
doesn't try to kill everybody.

523
00:29:04,376 --> 00:29:05,901
Little Mr. Perfect here.

524
00:29:07,179 --> 00:29:09,512
Yeah, he was that guy.

525
00:29:09,748 --> 00:29:11,774
He got adopted by rich folks.

526
00:29:12,384 --> 00:29:15,047
He went to the top
schools, then a top college.

527
00:29:15,120 --> 00:29:17,851
Meanwhile, I got
dragged to the circus

528
00:29:17,923 --> 00:29:19,824
by my depressed,
alcoholic mother.

529
00:29:19,992 --> 00:29:22,393
Forced to clean up
elephant dung every day.

530
00:29:22,461 --> 00:29:23,656
MAN: Who cares?

531
00:29:24,663 --> 00:29:27,098
Do you know how big
those things are, folks?

532
00:29:28,800 --> 00:29:31,235
But I know something
that Mommy and Daddy,

533
00:29:32,738 --> 00:29:33,933
they never knew.

534
00:29:36,341 --> 00:29:38,776
You're as crazy as I am.

535
00:29:43,615 --> 00:29:44,776
- No.
- (CROWD MURMURING)

536
00:29:46,652 --> 00:29:48,416
It's in your DNA.

537
00:29:51,657 --> 00:29:52,818
See,

538
00:29:53,959 --> 00:29:56,485
we got the same blood
running through us.

539
00:29:56,828 --> 00:29:59,957
We are practically identical.

540
00:30:00,565 --> 00:30:02,591
You are a killer.

541
00:30:04,169 --> 00:30:05,569
It's your nature.

542
00:30:07,673 --> 00:30:09,335
Stop trying to fight it.

543
00:30:22,688 --> 00:30:24,054
Take your best shot.

544
00:30:29,861 --> 00:30:30,861
(ROARS)

545
00:30:33,799 --> 00:30:35,165
Hey, what the hell happened?

546
00:30:35,334 --> 00:30:36,461
Snipers are dead.

547
00:30:36,535 --> 00:30:38,333
Get up on the roof,
take as many as you can.

548
00:30:38,403 --> 00:30:40,448
All right, just know a bunch of
chemicals are heading this way.

549
00:30:40,472 --> 00:30:42,566
Scarecrow had the
Wayne chemists mix it up.

550
00:30:44,976 --> 00:30:46,308
That's why he's been stalling.

551
00:30:46,378 --> 00:30:47,710
He wants a big crowd.

552
00:30:47,813 --> 00:30:49,873
He's gonna release the
laughing gas right here.

553
00:30:50,048 --> 00:30:51,744
We need to evacuate the area.

554
00:30:51,850 --> 00:30:53,284
Get these people out of here.

555
00:30:53,352 --> 00:30:55,548
Do whatever you have
to. Get them out of here.

556
00:30:55,954 --> 00:30:57,946
Time to kill this
maniac once and for all.

557
00:31:00,692 --> 00:31:01,692
(CROWD GASPING)

558
00:31:01,827 --> 00:31:05,355
JEROME: That was
so good! I love you.

559
00:31:10,535 --> 00:31:11,615
- (GUN COCKING)
- (GUNSHOTS)

560
00:31:31,556 --> 00:31:32,556
(BUTTON CLICKS)

561
00:31:32,724 --> 00:31:33,724
(STATIC BUZZ)

562
00:31:36,395 --> 00:31:37,395
(GRUNTS)

563
00:31:40,632 --> 00:31:42,312
- (CROWD SCREAMING)
- (LAUGHING MANIACALLY)

564
00:31:44,102 --> 00:31:46,401
WOMAN: Hey, hey!
Look! Up in the sky!

565
00:32:00,419 --> 00:32:01,419
(GROANS)

566
00:32:06,558 --> 00:32:07,558
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

567
00:32:16,268 --> 00:32:17,268
Holy crap.

568
00:32:18,470 --> 00:32:21,099
Excuse me, sir.
Could you help me?

569
00:32:21,206 --> 00:32:23,437
No can do, sport.

570
00:32:23,542 --> 00:32:27,070
Gotta get this rig into
position for the boss.

571
00:32:27,846 --> 00:32:29,109
And where is that?

572
00:32:29,481 --> 00:32:31,347
Paisley Square.

573
00:32:32,150 --> 00:32:34,517
Almost there.

574
00:32:34,753 --> 00:32:36,779
Then I can drop the load

575
00:32:36,855 --> 00:32:38,983
with this lever.

576
00:32:43,462 --> 00:32:45,658
You turn this thing
around right now!

577
00:32:45,764 --> 00:32:46,993
Can you not see that...

578
00:32:47,799 --> 00:32:49,631
Like I said, pal,

579
00:32:49,701 --> 00:32:52,330
no can do.

580
00:32:59,277 --> 00:33:00,277
(CROWD SCREAMING)

581
00:33:09,921 --> 00:33:10,980
JEROME: <i>It's coming.</i>

582
00:33:11,823 --> 00:33:13,121
Get into position.

583
00:33:18,763 --> 00:33:20,026
HARVEY: Holy moly.

584
00:33:22,000 --> 00:33:23,491
Holy moly.

585
00:33:24,669 --> 00:33:26,297
Jim, are you seeing this?

586
00:33:26,371 --> 00:33:28,169
Yeah, get everyone out of here.

587
00:33:28,273 --> 00:33:29,468
<i>I'm going after Jerome.</i>

588
00:33:30,008 --> 00:33:31,806
I can take it down with a shot.

589
00:33:32,043 --> 00:33:33,841
And risk spilling the chemicals?

590
00:33:34,479 --> 00:33:35,674
Oh, yeah, right.

591
00:33:42,220 --> 00:33:43,220
(CELL PHONE RINGING)

592
00:33:43,855 --> 00:33:44,879
Oswald?

593
00:33:44,990 --> 00:33:46,424
<i>Jim! Jim, help me.</i>

594
00:33:46,591 --> 00:33:49,652
They knocked me out,
and now I am in some blimp

595
00:33:49,728 --> 00:33:51,219
with that horrible gas.

596
00:33:51,329 --> 00:33:53,161
And the pilot, he's
been hypnotized.

597
00:33:53,265 --> 00:33:54,265
(STUTTERING)

598
00:33:54,432 --> 00:33:55,491
You're on the blimp?

599
00:33:55,567 --> 00:33:57,900
Yes. Yes, you have to help me.

600
00:33:58,770 --> 00:34:01,296
No, you're gonna help us.

601
00:34:02,007 --> 00:34:03,202
You're near the river.

602
00:34:03,308 --> 00:34:04,833
I need you to
steer it over there.

603
00:34:06,745 --> 00:34:08,714
Steer a blimp?

604
00:34:09,714 --> 00:34:11,580
Are you out of your mind, Jim?

605
00:34:11,683 --> 00:34:13,379
I don't even drive my own car.

606
00:34:13,685 --> 00:34:16,177
If you don't, thousands
will die. Maybe worse.

607
00:34:16,988 --> 00:34:18,354
What's worse than that?

608
00:34:18,423 --> 00:34:22,019
How can you run an empire
in a city full of lunatics?

609
00:34:29,501 --> 00:34:30,525
Hands up.

610
00:34:33,071 --> 00:34:34,972
Beautiful, isn't she?

611
00:34:37,943 --> 00:34:38,943
(BLIMP HOVERING)

612
00:34:40,745 --> 00:34:41,872
Just give me a second.

613
00:34:42,414 --> 00:34:44,576
Gotta call Tyler, tell
him he's in position.

614
00:34:44,950 --> 00:34:45,950
(GROANS)

615
00:34:46,918 --> 00:34:48,318
<i>Yes?</i>

616
00:34:48,420 --> 00:34:50,321
- Not cool.
- TYLER: <i>Jerome?</i>

617
00:34:51,122 --> 00:34:52,215
<i>Jerome?</i>

618
00:34:52,290 --> 00:34:54,225
<i>I'm in position...</i>

619
00:34:54,292 --> 00:34:55,885
(CHUCKLING) Doesn't matter.

620
00:34:58,330 --> 00:34:59,889
Too late anyway.

621
00:34:59,965 --> 00:35:00,965
Bombs away!

622
00:35:04,302 --> 00:35:05,302
(GASPING)

623
00:35:08,607 --> 00:35:09,631
Funny.

624
00:35:15,246 --> 00:35:16,270
No!

625
00:35:16,781 --> 00:35:17,781
(BOTH GRUNTING)

626
00:35:21,086 --> 00:35:22,086
(CROWD SCREAMING)

627
00:35:32,831 --> 00:35:33,831
PENGUIN: Come on.

628
00:35:35,767 --> 00:35:36,860
Now, come on.

629
00:35:36,968 --> 00:35:38,834
Up! Up! Up!

630
00:35:44,342 --> 00:35:45,833
Oh, okay. All right.

631
00:35:45,944 --> 00:35:48,106
Okay, okay. Okay...

632
00:35:48,179 --> 00:35:51,149
River. River...
Where is the river?

633
00:35:57,555 --> 00:35:59,023
Quite the dilemma, Jim.

634
00:35:59,858 --> 00:36:02,157
Are you gonna let
me fall and die...

635
00:36:02,627 --> 00:36:03,627
(GROANING)

636
00:36:04,062 --> 00:36:06,497
Or are you gonna pull
me up and arrest me?

637
00:36:09,668 --> 00:36:10,829
What's it gonna be?

638
00:36:13,872 --> 00:36:16,967
A lawman or a murderer?

639
00:36:25,050 --> 00:36:26,050
(GRUNTING)

640
00:36:28,119 --> 00:36:29,451
Good old Gordon.

641
00:36:29,521 --> 00:36:31,547
Always playing by the rules.

642
00:36:32,857 --> 00:36:34,792
That's why I'll outlive you.

643
00:36:36,061 --> 00:36:37,552
That's why I'm loved,

644
00:36:37,729 --> 00:36:40,062
'cause I don't give a
damn about the rules.

645
00:36:41,166 --> 00:36:42,896
It's a long way down.

646
00:36:43,001 --> 00:36:44,663
You sure you'll outlive me?

647
00:36:44,736 --> 00:36:46,227
Oh, I'm sure.

648
00:36:46,604 --> 00:36:48,766
'Cause I'm more than a man.

649
00:36:48,873 --> 00:36:52,002
I'm an idea, a philosophy.

650
00:36:52,343 --> 00:36:54,437
And I will live on
in the shadows,

651
00:36:54,546 --> 00:36:56,879
within Gotham's discontent.

652
00:37:02,220 --> 00:37:03,848
You'll be seeing me soon.

653
00:37:04,255 --> 00:37:05,255
<i>Au revoir.</i>

654
00:37:05,757 --> 00:37:06,757
(LAUGHING MANIACALLY)

655
00:37:11,763 --> 00:37:13,425
(THUDDING)

656
00:37:26,044 --> 00:37:27,774
WOMAN: Never
thought I'd see this.

657
00:37:27,879 --> 00:37:29,404
MAN: Sure he's
dead. I can't believe.

658
00:37:29,514 --> 00:37:30,607
Is he?

659
00:37:30,715 --> 00:37:32,047
Yeah.

660
00:37:33,785 --> 00:37:34,844
GORDON: Get back.

661
00:37:35,520 --> 00:37:37,455
GCPD. Everybody get back.

662
00:38:08,453 --> 00:38:09,580
Mr. Valeska.

663
00:38:11,923 --> 00:38:15,087
I meant what I said about your
work being of importance to the city.

664
00:38:16,961 --> 00:38:19,430
Let Wayne Enterprises
fund your work with a grant.

665
00:38:24,302 --> 00:38:25,565
Thank you.

666
00:38:39,684 --> 00:38:40,845
Captain.

667
00:38:44,389 --> 00:38:45,389
(CELL PHONE RINGING)

668
00:38:48,893 --> 00:38:49,986
Oswald.

669
00:38:50,161 --> 00:38:51,161
Um...

670
00:38:51,396 --> 00:38:52,625
Hello.

671
00:38:52,697 --> 00:38:53,858
Still here.

672
00:38:54,132 --> 00:38:57,227
Will someone please get
me the hell off this thing?

673
00:39:00,171 --> 00:39:01,332
We're on it.

674
00:39:04,309 --> 00:39:06,835
How do we get a blimp
down safely from over a river?

675
00:39:06,911 --> 00:39:08,072
You asking me?

676
00:39:08,179 --> 00:39:10,739
I say we let him stew up
there for a few more hours.

677
00:39:12,784 --> 00:39:14,810
We'll get a hold
of the standby pilot.

678
00:39:15,019 --> 00:39:17,181
<i>Have him advise.
Sit tight, all right?</i>

679
00:39:17,455 --> 00:39:18,455
Oh!

680
00:39:18,823 --> 00:39:20,314
And Oswald Cobblepot,

681
00:39:21,159 --> 00:39:22,491
Gotham thanks you.

682
00:39:22,694 --> 00:39:24,060
Wait, Jim. Jim?

683
00:39:24,863 --> 00:39:26,661
Jim? Jim.

684
00:39:26,998 --> 00:39:28,227
Jim!

685
00:39:28,666 --> 00:39:30,794
Jim!

686
00:39:35,707 --> 00:39:36,707
(TABITHA GRUNTING)

687
00:39:38,877 --> 00:39:40,539
Never touch me again.

688
00:39:40,912 --> 00:39:43,108
Ms. Kean has a
new path to take now.

689
00:39:43,348 --> 00:39:45,681
- It no longer involves you.
- Is that so?

690
00:39:45,750 --> 00:39:48,242
We will accept you leaving
this city and never coming back.

691
00:39:48,720 --> 00:39:51,189
The only thing I'll accept
is you kissing my ass.

692
00:39:51,256 --> 00:39:53,248
We have been trained
by the League of Shadows

693
00:39:53,358 --> 00:39:56,760
in 90 different forms of combat
since we were five years old.

694
00:39:56,861 --> 00:39:59,194
Oh, yeah? Which one of
you bitches wants to go first?

695
00:40:00,031 --> 00:40:01,031
(GRUNTING)

696
00:40:15,513 --> 00:40:17,744
Next time, we kill you.

697
00:40:37,902 --> 00:40:39,097
Let me help you.

698
00:40:44,409 --> 00:40:45,409
(GROANING)

699
00:40:48,279 --> 00:40:49,279
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

700
00:40:50,315 --> 00:40:51,578
Who the hell are you guys?

701
00:40:51,916 --> 00:40:54,511
The ones that have been
watching you and Barbara Kean,

702
00:40:54,619 --> 00:40:56,588
the impostor, for
quite some time.

703
00:40:57,188 --> 00:40:59,248
We serve the one
and only true master,

704
00:40:59,357 --> 00:41:00,825
Ra's al Ghul.

705
00:41:01,592 --> 00:41:02,855
But he's dead.

706
00:41:03,962 --> 00:41:05,453
Death is only an illusion.

707
00:42:18,536 --> 00:42:19,536
(LAUGHING MANIACALLY)

708
00:42:25,476 --> 00:42:26,476
(COUGHING)

709
00:42:29,313 --> 00:42:31,509
JEROME: <i>Hello, brother.</i>

710
00:42:31,582 --> 00:42:35,644
<i>Didn't think you can get
rid of me so easily, did you?</i>

711
00:42:35,720 --> 00:42:39,589
<i>See, my days were
numbered, but you...</i>

712
00:42:40,858 --> 00:42:43,589
<i>Oh, you can continue on for me.</i>

713
00:42:43,694 --> 00:42:45,890
<i>Be my ultimate revenge.</i>

714
00:42:45,997 --> 00:42:50,560
<i>So, calm yourself.
Don't fight it.</i>

715
00:42:50,635 --> 00:42:52,467
<i>Breathe it in.</i>

716
00:42:52,570 --> 00:42:55,631
<i>This gas was a special
mixture I had made</i>

717
00:42:55,740 --> 00:42:57,436
<i>just for you.</i>

718
00:42:57,542 --> 00:43:00,706
<i>Something to
finally set you free.</i>

719
00:43:01,279 --> 00:43:03,908
<i>- It's time to have some fun.</i>
- (LAUGHING MANIACALLY)

720
00:43:03,981 --> 00:43:06,416
<i>Burn it down, brother.</i>

721
00:43:06,484 --> 00:43:08,749
<i>Burn it all down.</i>

722
00:43:49,927 --> 00:43:50,927
English - SDH
